{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "DenyUnencryptedUploads",
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::acme-financial-reports/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringNotEquals": {
          "s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption": "aws:kms"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "Sid": "DenyHTTP",
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::acme-financial-reports/*",
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {
          "aws:SecureTransport": "false"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

Explanation: Default encryption (set via bucket properties) ensures that objects uploaded without encryption headers get encrypted with the designated KMS key. The bucket policy acts as a guard: it explicitly denies any upload that doesn't request SSE‑KMS, and also blocks non‑HTTPS traffic. Together they provide defense in depth.
